<hr />
<h2>PHASE 11 — ACTION PLAN</h2>
<h3>TOP 10 THINGS TO FIX FIRST</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Implement Proper Authentication (Priority: Critical | Effort: Med | Impact: High)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>app.py</code>, <code>templates/index.html</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Implement Flask-Session or JWTs to secure <code>/dashboard</code> and prevent direct URL access.</li>
<li><strong>Fix Plaintext Passwords (Priority: Critical | Effort: Low | Impact: High)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>app.py</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Use <code>werkzeug.security.generate_password_hash</code> and <code>check_password_hash</code> for registration and login.</li>
<li><strong>Secure Password Reset (Priority: Critical | Effort: Med | Impact: High)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>app.py</code>, <code>templates/forgot_password.html</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Require the old password to change it, or implement secure email token links.</li>
<li><strong>Fix Missing NLTK Dependencies (Priority: High | Effort: Low | Impact: High)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>app.py</code>, <code>requirements.txt</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Add <code>nltk</code> to requirements. Add <code>nltk.download('punkt_tab')</code> and <code>stopwords</code> to app initialization.</li>
<li><strong>Fix the Data Leakage Bug in Features (Priority: High | Effort: Low | Impact: Med)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>app.py</code>, <code>utils/features.py</code>, <code>utils/preprocessing.py</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Extract the <code>has_url</code> feature before running <code>clean_text()</code>, otherwise it will always be 0.</li>
<li><strong>Migrate away from CSV (Priority: High | Effort: Med | Impact: High)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>app.py</code>, <code>users.csv</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Replace the flat file with a SQLite database using <code>Flask-SQLAlchemy</code> to prevent race conditions.</li>
<li><strong>Fix Malformed HTML (Priority: Med | Effort: Low | Impact: Med)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>templates/index.html</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Remove the duplicated <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> document block.</li>
<li><strong>Fix Hardcoded Paths (Priority: Med | Effort: Low | Impact: Low)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>app.py</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Consistently use the <code>BASE_DIR</code> logic for file referencing.</li>
<li><strong>Restore Datasets (Priority: High | Effort: Low | Impact: High)</strong></li>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>datasets/</code> (Create it)</li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Upload the missing <code>email_dataset.csv</code> so the model can be retrained.</li>
<li><strong>Implement Real Testing (Priority: Med | Effort: High | Impact: High)</strong><ul>
<li><em>Files:</em> <code>test_features.py</code>, <code>test_preprocessing.py</code></li>
<li><em>Action:</em> Convert the print scripts into a proper <code>pytest</code> suite testing all utility functions and API routes.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<h3>Roadmap</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Immediate Fixes (Today):</strong> Fix the NLTK crashes, add NLTK to requirements, fix the broken <code>index.html</code> file, and implement basic Flask sessions so the dashboard isn't completely open to the public. Hash passwords.</li>
<li><strong>Short-Term Improvements (This Week):</strong> Fix the feature extraction logic bug. Replace the CSV with SQLite. Secure the <code>forgot-password</code> route.</li>
<li><strong>Medium-Term Improvements (This Month):</strong> Locate and upload the missing dataset. Write a comprehensive <code>pytest</code> suite. Refactor the frontend to use a single, consistent CSS framework.</li>
<li><strong>Long-Term Improvements (Future):</strong> Move away from basic <code>LogisticRegression</code> and keyword counts to a more robust NLP model (like a small transformer or TF-IDF pipeline). Containerize the application with Docker.</li>
</ul>
